claim.claim-text:
receiving the base on a platform;
detecting a first depth of a first cavity on the base with a sensing device, which optionally is an optical sensing device;
receiving an image file of a structure to be formed on the base;
wherein the image file includes a predetermined thickness of a layer;
generating a modified image file using the first depth, wherein the modified image file includes a first adjusted thickness for a portion of the layer corresponding to the first cavity; and
printing a base layer directly onto the base using the modified image file, wherein the base layer includes a first adjusted portion printed within the first cavity, wherein the first adjusted portion has the first adjusted thickness and the base layer includes a non-adjusted portion printed onto the base, wherein the non-adjusted portion has the predetermined thickness.

receiving an image file <co>rresponding to a two-dimensional representation of the three-dimensional structure, wherein the image file includes a predetermined thickness of a layer;
receiving the base having a first cavity with a first depth and a second cavity with a second depth;
detecting the first depth of the first cavity and detecting the second depth of the second cavity with a sensing device, wherein the second depth is greater than the first depth;
generating a modified image file using the first depth and the second depth, wherein the modified image file includes a first adjusted thickness of a first portion of the layer corresponding to the first cavity and a second adjusted thickness of a second portion of the layer corresponding to the second cavity;
printing a base layer directly onto the base using the modified image file, wherein the base layer includes a first adjusted portion printed within the first cavity and a first non-adjusted portion printed onto the base;
wherein the first adjusted portion has the first adjusted thickness and fills the first cavity and the first non-adjusted portion has the predetermined thickness;
wherein an upper surface of the first adjusted portion is continuous with an upper surface of the first non-adjusted portion; and
wherein the base layer further includes a second adjusted portion printed within the second cavity, wherein the second adjusted portion has the second adjusted thickness and partially fills the second cavity thereby forming a third cavity that extends from an upper surface of the base layer to an upper surface of the second adjusted portion.

a control system <c>onfigured to:
receive information about a depth of a cavity on a surface of the base;
receive an image file of a structure having a predetermined thickness of a layer to be printed on the base;
adjust the image file based on the depth of the cavity and generate an adjusted image file having an adjusted thickness for a portion of the layer corresponding to the cavity;
transmit the adjusted image file to a printing device; and
